extends ../../../layouts/master.pug

block title
  title NBC - Associate of Arts in Ministry

block header
  include ../../../components/header.pug

block content
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.nav-breadcrums.bg-gray-100
      .container
        .breadcrumb
          ul
            li.home
              a(href='/index-4.html') Home
            li
              a(href='/programs/') Programs
            li
              span A.A. in Ministry
  section.section-box
    .banner-hero.banner-head-image(style='background: url(/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_332409626.jpeg); background-size: cover; background-position: center bottom;')
      .container
        .text-center
          h1.text-heading-1.color-white.mt-30
            | Associate of Arts in Ministry
  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h2#overview.text-heading-4 Two Year College Degree
            p.text-body-text
              | The Associate of Arts in Ministry degree is designed to provide students with a solid foundation in Bible, theology, and ministry principles. This two-year program prepares students for entry-level ministry positions, lay leadership roles, and provides a strong foundation for those who plan to continue their education toward a bachelor's degree.
        .row
          .col-lg-12
            .row
              .col-lg-6
                h2#majors.text-heading-4.mt-30 Program Focus
                p.text-body-text
                  | The Associate of Arts in Ministry (A.A.Min.) degree provides a comprehensive foundation in biblical studies, theology, and practical ministry skills. This program is ideal for students who want to:
                ul
                  li Begin their ministry education with a focused two-year program
                  li Prepare for entry-level ministry positions
                  li Build a strong foundation before pursuing a bachelor's degree
                  li Develop practical ministry skills for lay leadership roles
                  li Gain a solid understanding of Bible and theology

              .col-lg-6.d-flex.justify-content-center.flex-column
                img.img-responsive.bdr-10.mt-10.ml-10(src='/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_554620518.jpeg', alt='Agon')

              .border-bottom.mt-50

  section.section-box.overflow-visible.mb-50
    .container
      .row
        .col-lg-10.mx-auto
          .bg-6.box-newsletter.position-relative
            .content-detail
              span.text-body-capitalized.color-gray-500.text-uppercase degree requirements
              h4.text-heading-2.mb-10.mt-10 Traditional Degree Structure
              p.text-body-text.color-gray-500
              | The associate degree in the traditional degree structure at Nazarene Bible College contains the following degree requirements:
              ul
                li Completion of a minimum of 64 semester hours.
                li At least 32 semester hours in residence–with at least 16 of the final 32 hours in residence. Online classes are considered “in residence.”
                li A cumulative GPA of at least 2.0 (on a 4.0 scale).
                li Completion of the required hours in the following areas:
                  ul
                    li General Education
                    li Bible and Theology
                    li Major Concentration
                li Completion of NBC Experience
                li College indebtedness paid in full.

  section.section-box
    .container.mt-120
      .row
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-12.block-img-we-do
          img.bdrd-16.img-responsive(src='/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_356337517.jpeg', alt='Agon')
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-12.block-we-do
          span.tag-1.bg-6.color-green-900 Core Requirements and Objectives
          h3.text-heading-1.mt-30 General Education Core
          p.text-body-text.color-gray-600.mt-30
            | Through General Education, Nazarene Bible College encourages the acquisition of foundational knowledge, skills, and values essential for Lifelong Learning and preparation for in-depth study within chosen majors. Students will experience courses in four areas of study: Spiritual Foundations, Communication, Basic Knowledge, and Social Science/Humanities.
          h4.text-heading-4.mt-30 Faculty
          ul
            li Dr. Sandra Palm, Director
            li Dr. Robbin Trumble
      .row.mt-50.mb-50
        .col-lg-12
          p.text-body-lead-large.color-gray-600
            | Completion of the General Education core should enable students to:
          .line-bd-green.mt-30.mb-30
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Engage in intentional spiritual growth toward a Christ-like character and life of service.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Demonstrate effective communication skills.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Exhibit an understanding of the scientific method and mathematical principles.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Analyze traditional and evolving views of women, race, and ethnicity in the US and abroad.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Examine civilization in a global context with emphasis on the history of Christianity and evangelism.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Apply the basic principles of Christian ethics in modern society.

  section.section-box.mt-50.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h3.text-heading-4.mb-20 Core Requirements and Objectives
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h4.text-heading-5.mb-20 General Education Core
            p.text-body-text
              strong Objectives
            p.text-body-text
              | Through General Education, Nazarene Bible College encourages the acquisition of foundational knowledge, skills, and values essential for Lifelong Learning and preparation for in-depth study within chosen majors. Students will experience courses in four areas of study: Spiritual Foundations, Communication, Basic Knowledge, and Social Science/Humanities
            p.text-body-text
              | Completion of the General Education core should enable students to:
              ul
                li Engage in intentional spiritual growth toward a Christ-like character and life of service.
                li Demonstrate effective communication skills.
                li Exhibit an understanding of the scientific method and mathematical principles.
                li Analyze traditional and evolving views of women, race, and ethnicity in the US. and abroad.
                li Examine civilization in a global context with emphasis on the history of Christianity and evangelism.
                li Apply the basic principles of Christian ethics in modern society.
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h4.text-heading-5.mb-20 General Education Core Courses
            p.text-body-text
              | The student will take either the English Composition I and II sequence or the Basic English Skills courses* followed by the English Composition I and II sequence after placement testing.
            table.table.table-striped
              thead
                tr
                  th Course
                  th Course Description
                  th Hours
              tbody
                +CourseTableRow('PAS-1013', 'Introduction to Christian Service', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('PAS-1023', 'Spiritual Formation', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('THE-3013', 'Introduction to Christian Thought', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('ENG-1013', 'English Composition I', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('ENG-1023', 'English Composition II', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('SPE-1003', 'Principles of Public Speaking', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('GEN-1003', 'Lifelong Learning Skills', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('MTH-1003', 'General Mathematics', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('SCI-2013', 'General Physical Science', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('PSY-1013', 'Introduction to Psychology', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('HIS-2013', 'Western World/Ancient & Medieval Times', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('HIS-2023', 'Western World/Emerging Modern Society', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('PHI-3013', 'Philosophy and Christian Ethics', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('ENG-1043', 'Classical Literature', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('SOC-1003', 'Introduction to Sociology', '3')
              tfoot
                tr
                  td
                  td
                  td
                    strong 45 hours
        .row
          .box-info.col-lg-10.bg-gray-100.mx-auto
            p.text-body-text
              | *The Basic English Skills sequence is not included in the requirements for a degree program. Students who are required to take Basic English Skills courses will complete a minimum of 63 or 71 hours for a degree, depending on the major.

  section.section-box
    .container.mt-120
      .row
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-12.block-img-we-do
          img.bdrd-16.img-responsive(src='/assets/imgs/stock/AdobeStock_554620960.jpeg', alt='Agon')
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-12.block-we-do
          span.tag-1.bg-6.color-green-900 Objectives
          h3.text-heading-1.mt-30 Bible and Theology Core
          h4.text-heading-4.mt-30 Faculty
          ul
            li Dr. Thomas King, Director
      .row.mt-50.mb-50
        .col-lg-12
          p.text-body-lead-large.color-gray-600
            | Completion of the Bible and Theology core should enable students to:
          .line-bd-green.mt-30.mb-30
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Identify the basic content of the Bible.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Utilize sound methods and resources for interpreting the Bible.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Articulate the essentials of the Christian faith.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Nurture the Christlike life as informed by Scripture and Christian thought.
        .col-lg-6.col-sm-6.col-12.mt-15
          p.text-body-excerpt.color-gray-600.icon-triangle Apply a Christian worldview to contemporary critical issues.

  section.section-box.mb-50.mt-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h4.text-heading-5.mb-20.text-center Bible and Theology Core Courses
            table.table.table-striped
              thead
                tr
                  th Course
                  th Course Description
                  th Hours
              tbody
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-1013', 'Introduction to the Old Testament', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-1023', 'Introduction to the New Testament', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-2003', 'Biblical Interpretation', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-2013', 'Pentateuch', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('BIB-2033', 'New Testament Gospels', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('THE-2013', 'Doctrine of Holiness', '3')
                +CourseTableRow('THE-3023', 'Systematic Theology I', '3')
              tfoot
                tr
                  td 
                  td 
                  td 
                    strong 21 hours
        .row
          .box-info.col-lg-10.bg-gray-100.mx-auto
            p.text-body-text
              | In addition to the Bible and Theology Core Courses, traditional degree students are to complete the ABHE Bible Content Exam at the beginning and at the end of their degree. The exam results are used to assess student learning in the area of Bible content.

  section.section-box.mb-50
    .container
      .content-detail
        .row
          .col-lg-2
          .col-lg-8
            h3.text-heading-4.mb-20 Academic Assessment Report (Student Outcomes)
            p.text-body-text Nazarene Bible College annually assesses the effectiveness of its academic programs. A report of the annual academic assessment process is accessible below.

